.TH EUCLID-CLI-EKV-DESCRIBE-TABLE 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.73" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ekv-describe-table \- show a table's key and size
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ekv describe-table
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I TABLE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints what a table is keyed on, its ERN, when it was created, and how
many items it holds.
.PP
The item count is counted when you ask rather than kept in the table's
record. That costs a query against the table and means the number is
always right; a stored counter would be cheaper and would drift.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fITABLE\fR
Table name. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The description is printed.
.TP
.B 1
No table of that name exists in this account.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli ekv describe-table --name deliveries
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ekv (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekv-create-table (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekv-list-tables (1)
